  "raw_text": "10\n\nDICTIONARY / DICCIONARIO\n\n(Blue font indicates that verification or other work still to be done in this area. /\n\nLa fuente azul\n \nindica que aún debe realizarse la verificación u otro trabajo en esta área.)\n\nAbakaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto overturn, to capsize, to shipwreck\n \n/ volcar, naufragar\n\nAbakuk\n \n(\ndb,dba\n;\n \nHabaku\n-bw\n;\n \nHabacuc\n-dbta\n)\n \n–\n \nHabakkuk\n \n(Bible book) / Habacuc (libro bíblico)\n\nAba\nl\nkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto mix, to stir\n \n/\n \nmezclar, revolver\n, batir\n\nAbdías\n \n(Abdias)\n \n(\ndb,db\nt\na\n;\n \nObadaia\n-\nbw,dba\n)\n \n–\n \nObadiah\n \n(Bible book)\n \n/\n \nAbd\nía\ns\n \n(libro bíblico)\n\nAdar\n \n(a/t:\n \nAda\n,\n \nArder\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \norder\n, command\n \n/ orden,\n \nmandato\n\nAdar briaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto receive orders\n, to receive commands\n \n/\n \nrecibir pedidos, recibir comandos\n\nAdar munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto order, to command\n \n/ ordenar, mandar, pedir\n\nAdar mamunra\n \n(n-agent/s-agente)\n \n–\n \none who gives orders, one who gives commands\n \n/ uno que da\nórdenes\n\nAdar raya\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nnew order, new command\n \n/ nuevo orden, nuevo mandato\n\nAdar yabaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto give an order, to give a command\n \n/ dar una orden, dar un mandato\n\nAhkia\n?\n \n–\n \nW\nhen\n?\n \n/\n \n¿\nCu\ná\nndo?\n \n(See\n \nalso/ Ver también:\n \nA\nhkia piua ra\n?, Ani piua ra?\n)\n\n(\nEx/Ej:\n \nAhkia wan?\n \n–\n \nWhen did he/she/they go?\n \n/\n \n¿\nCuándo\n \nse\n \nfu\né\n \nél/ella/ellos\n/ellas\n?\n)\n\nAhkia ahkia\n \n–\n \nwhenever\n, anytime\n \n/\n \nen cua\nlquier momento\n, cuando quiera que\n\nAhkia piua ra?\n \n–\n \nAt what\n \ntime?\n, When?\n \n/ ¿A qué hora?, ¿\nC\nuándo?\n\n(ExEj\n \n(\nwqu\n-\n04/20\n):\n \nJoel 2:28,29 aisi ba ahkia piua ra aimakan ki?\n \n–\n \nWhen\n \nwas Joel 2:28,29 fulfilled?\n \n/\n \n¿\nCuando\n \nse cumplió\n\nJoel 2:28,29?\n)\n\nAhkia kat?\n \n–\n \nUntil when?\n \n/ ¿Hasta cuándo?\n\nAi\n \n(1)\n \n–\n \nher, his, its, their\n \n/ su, sus, suyo, suyos\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nAi uplika\n \n–\n \nhis/her/their/its people\n \n/ su gente)\n\nAi\n \n(2)\n \n–\n \nme\n, to me\n,\n \nself\n, myself\n \n/\n \nyo, a mí, yo mismo\n\n(Note\n/Nota\n:\n \nAi\n \nwith a verb can\n \nindicate that the object of that verb is\n \nme\n.\n \n/\n \nAi\n \ncon un verbo puede indicar que el objeto de ese\n\nverbo soy\n \n“yo”.\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nKunin ai munram\n \n–\n \nYou tricked me\n \n/ Me engañaste)\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nmwb\n):\n \nNaha wikka Baibil aisi kaikanka ba Jehova dukiara dîa ai smalkisa?\n \n–\n \nWhat did this week’s Bible reading teach you\n\nabout Jehovah?\n \n/ ¿Qué te enseñó la lectura bíblica de esta semana acerca de Jehová?)\n\nAikaia\n \n(v-irregularity of / irregularidad de:\n \nYabaia\n \n–\n \nto give\n \n/ dar; See also/ Ver también:\n \nMaikaia\n \n&\n \nWankaia\n)\n \n–\n\nto give me, to allow me, to cause me\n \n/ darme, permitirme, causarme\n \n(See entry below/ Ver entrada debajo:\n\nAikaia\n)\n\nAi wis\n \n(v-imp)\n \n–\n \ntell me\n \n/ dime, digame, diganme\n\nÂ\ni\naibapra\n \n(Aiaibapra)\n \n(see\n/ver\n:\n \nAibapaia\n)\n \n(n\n-\nagent/s\n-\nagente)\n \n–\n \npayer, one who pays\n \n/\n \npagador,\n \nuno\n \nque paga\n\nÂialkra\n \n(see/ver:\n \nAlkaia\n) (n-agent/s-agente) (\ndict, db-Aiseya 22:15\n, not in / no en:\n \ndictu\n)\n \n–\n \nholder, captor, catcher\n \n/\ntitular, captor, receptor\n\nInska âialkra\n \n(n-agent/s-agente)\n \n–\n \nfisherman\n \n/ pescador\n\nÂiamra\n \n(Aiamra)\n \n(see/ver:\n \nAmaia\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nsomeone who burns, something that is combustible, something that is flammable\n\n/ alguien que quema, algo que es combustible, algo que es inflamable\n\nÂiauhbra\n \n(see/ver:\n \nAuhbaia\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nperson or thing that fills, stores, packs, loads, or stuffs\n \n/ persona o cosa que llena,\nalmacena, empaca, o carga\n\nAiawaia\n \n(\ndb,dict\n;\n \nAiauaia\n-dictu,dict-alt\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto move oneself\n \n/ moverse\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nlfb57\n):\n \nJirimaya tihmia aiska sip aiawras kan\n \n–\n \nJeremiah was not able to move all night\n \n/ Jeremías no pudo moverse en toda\nla noche)\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\ndb-1Sam 12:16\n):\n \nnanara buisma ba kat ban bûi bas, aiawpara\n \n–\n \nnow continue to be standing where you are standing, do not\nmove\n \n/ ahora\n \nsigan parados donde están parados, no se muevan)\n\nAiawanka\n \n(a/t:\n \nAiauanka\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nmovement of the body\n \n/ movimiento del cuerpo\n\nAiawikira\n \n(a/t:\n \nAiauikira\n) (adj,adv)\n \n–\n \nactive, actively, moving, in motion\n \n/ activo, activamente, en movimiento\n\nAibanhwaia\n \n(see/ver:\n \nBanhwaia\n)\n\nAibapaia\n \n(1) (v)\n \n–\n \nto pay\n \n/ pagar",
